 "final_text": "Submitted January AP:\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `jan_erp_ap` | $13,800.00 |\n| `jan_workbook_ap` | $12,000.00 |\n| `jan_variance` | $1,800.00 |\n\n**Root cause:** the workbook was locked on Jan 27, before QINV-002 (\"January late-posted repair,\" $1,800, trans date 2026-01-28) hit the AP subledger. QINV-001 ($12,000) is the only invoice it captured. QINV-003 ($3,200) is correctly a February transaction and isn't part of either figure.\n\nReady for February whenever you want to continue.\n\n[step 02] Submitted:\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `feb_erp_ap` | $17,000.00 |\n| `feb_workbook_ap` | $13,800.00 |\n| `feb_variance` | $3,200.00 |\n| `jan_item_resolved` | yes |\n\nSummary: January's gap (QINV-002) is now folded into the workbook, as expected. But the same root cause recurred in February \u2014 QINV-003 ($3,200, dated 02-25) missed the 02-26 workbook cutoff, so the pattern of the workbook lagging late-posted invoices by a cutoff day is repeating month over month. Worth flagging to whoever preps the workbook: pull it a day later, or add a standing \"invoices posted in the last 48 hours\" check before locking each close.",
